<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Izamal</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Izamal is a town in the Mexican state of Yucatán, built over a large Maya city whose pyramids, among them Kinich Kak Moo, are some of the largest in the peninsula. A pilgrimage centre of the god <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/itzamna">Itzamna</a>, it belonged to the Chel province after the fall of Mayapan. In the 1550s the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/franciscans">Franciscans</a> built the Convent of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/san-antonio">San Antonio</a> de <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/padua">Padua</a> on top of one of its pyramids.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/izamal.jpg" alt="Izamal" width="320" height="323" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Addicted04 · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Izamal_collage.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
